{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02433",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.01,
      "end_seconds": 6.33,
      "duration_seconds": 5.32,
      "text": "Hi, doctor, I came as soon as they called me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.2,
      "end_seconds": 10.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Of course, leave it there. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.0,
      "end_seconds": 15.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "So, I've been feeling faint, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 15.83,
      "end_seconds": 27.7,
      "duration_seconds": 11.87,
      "text": "Okay, go on. Right, tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.66,
      "end_seconds": 43.79,
      "duration_seconds": 15.13,
      "text": "I get some relief from lying down. Pretty mild, if I'm being honest. I've also had a swollen tummy, for six months. With swollen tummy, pretty mild, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.16,
      "end_seconds": 48.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Any fever or chest pain at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 49.1,
      "end_seconds": 52.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "So, no, no fever or chest pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 53.27,
      "end_seconds": 57.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "I follow. Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.75,
      "end_seconds": 63.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.03,
      "end_seconds": 67.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "Your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.37,
      "end_seconds": 71.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "Actually, you know, no problems with breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 73.68,
      "end_seconds": 75.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.59,
      "end_seconds": 82.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "Nothing, I'm teetotal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.04,
      "end_seconds": 85.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Is there someone at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.47,
      "end_seconds": 91.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.19,
      "end_seconds": 93.81,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "How are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.34,
      "end_seconds": 98.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.92,
      "end_seconds": 118.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "Okay, any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.23,
      "end_seconds": 120.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.49,
      "text": "No surgery, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.84,
      "end_seconds": 123.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.15,
      "end_seconds": 126.76,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "Yes, heart failure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.78,
      "end_seconds": 134.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "Okay, go on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.09,
      "end_seconds": 152.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.74,
      "end_seconds": 156.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "My father has Parkinson's disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.62,
      "end_seconds": 161.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.59,
      "end_seconds": 167.62,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "Amoxicillin. I come out in... well, a rash all over."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.31,
      "end_seconds": 187.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "Do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.32,
      "end_seconds": 207.13,
      "duration_seconds": 18.81,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, it's carvedilol, 6.25 milligrams, twice a day. I take alcohol every day, daily. Uh, you know, I'd been on furosemide, not any more though, I stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 207.95,
      "end_seconds": 217.78,
      "duration_seconds": 9.83,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Temperature is 37.0 degrees, heart rate 106. BP is 102 over 57, oxygen saturation is 98 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.72,
      "end_seconds": 220.42,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.47,
      "end_seconds": 226.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "I'll examine you in a second, make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.36,
      "end_seconds": 232.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.02,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.28,
      "end_seconds": 235.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "Look straight ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.72,
      "end_seconds": 255.27,
      "duration_seconds": 7.55,
      "text": "You are yellow, your tummy is swollen with fluid, and your pulse is very fast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 257.35,
      "end_seconds": 258.29,
      "duration_seconds": 0.94,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.9,
      "end_seconds": 290.16,
      "duration_seconds": 28.26,
      "text": "All finished, thank you. Having listened and examined, my working impression is a bleed from enlarged veins in the gullet in liver disease. Another possibility is a bleeding ulcer. Let's get urgent blood tests, for major bleed. Let's get an urgent endoscopy, for variceal bleed. The treatment will be terlipressin, 2 milligrams, now, single dose. That's for variceal bleeding. You are going straight to resus, I am starting two drips."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.81,
      "end_seconds": 299.61,
      "duration_seconds": 8.8,
      "text": "Please take the tablets with food so they don't upset your stomach. I think the emergency team should see you too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 301.15,
      "end_seconds": 303.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Sure, where do I go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.45,
      "end_seconds": 318.16,
      "duration_seconds": 13.71,
      "text": "Keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency. Book a review straight away. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 319.75,
      "end_seconds": 324.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "Okay, you know, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 326.16,
      "end_seconds": 327.8,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "Have a good day."
    }
  ]
}